  "strategy": "1. Approach and rationale\nThe primary approach leverages a structured initialization with 5-fold symmetry to avoid local optima and employs a robust optimization technique to minimize the maximum overlap integral. This method addresses the non-convexity of the problem by combining a well-constructed starting point with an efficient optimizer. \n\n2. Mathematical specification\nDefine the step function \\( h: [0, 2] \\rightarrow [0, 1] \\) discretized into \\( n = 70 \\) points, with \\( dx = \\frac{2}{70} \\). The function \\( \\mathbf{h} = [h_i]_{i=1}^{70} \\) must satisfy \\( \\sum h_i = 35 \\) and \\( 0 \\leq h_i \\leq 1 \\).\n\nThe objective is to minimize:\n\\[ C_5 = \\max_k \\left( \\sum_{i=1}^{70 - |k|} h_i (1 - h_{i+|k|}) \\cdot dx \\right) \\]\nover all possible shifts \\( k \\in \\{-69, \\dots, 0, \\dots, 69\\} \\).\n\n3. Implementation procedure\n1. **Initialization**:\n   - Divide the 70 points into 5 segments of 14 points each.\n   - Set the first segment to 0.7, the second to 0.3, alternating for each segment.\n   - Adjust the entire array to ensure the sum is 35.\n\n2. **Optimization Loop**:\n   - Use L-BFGS-B for optimization with bounds [0, 1].\n   - After each iteration, perform feasibility repair:\n     - Clip \\( h \\) to [0, 1].\n     - Scale \\( h \\) such that \\( \\sum h_i = 35 \\).\n\n3. **Gradient Calculation**:\n   - Compute the gradient using central differences for accuracy.\n   - Consider only the shifts \\( k \\) that contribute to the current maximum overlap.\n\n4. **Stopping Criteria**:\n   - Terminate after 600 seconds or achieve \\( C_5 \\leq 0.3807 \\).\n\n4. Search choices and variations\n- Use a 5-fold symmetric initialization to ensure a balanced starting point.\n- Apply L-BFGS-B with default settings for efficiency and robustness.\n- Perform feasibility repair after each iteration to maintain constraints.\n\n5. Compute budget and robustness\n- Initialization: <1s.\n- Optimization loop: ~500s.\n- Feasibility repair: <1s per iteration.\n- Total: ~600s, ensuring timely termination if no improvement.\n\n6. Validation and return contract\n- Ensure \\( \\sum h_i = 35 \\).\n- Confirm all \\( h_i \\in [0, 1] \\).\n- Recompute \\( C_5 \\) to validate the result.",
